# VPN user access - one line per user (read by /etc/firewall/rc.openvpn):
#   <vpn user>  <n>  <host>[,<host>...]  <port/proto>[,...] | all
# The user always gets VPN address 172.30.98.<n> (UDP) / 172.30.99.<n> (TCP),
# a route to each host, and may reach only those hosts on those ports (plus
# ping). A host may be a network: 192.168.1.0/24 all = the whole LAN.
# n: 10-250, unique. A user not listed here cannot connect at all.
# Apply: sudo /etc/firewall/rc.openvpn   (takes effect at the next connection)
# Easier: sudo vpnuser add|set|del ...  (edits this file and applies it)
jane.doe             10  192.168.1.106   3389/tcp,3389/udp
john.roe             11  192.168.1.0/24  all
